              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ROOOKIES3"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is almost identical to my Grandmother's recipe. She always added in 1/4 cup chopped pecans and 1/2 cup coconut. My grandma always had them stored in her refrigerator ready to bake for when people dropped by. You will love this cookie!!! Debbie"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "New to Bypass"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I was looking for a recipe we made as a 4H cookie fifty years ago in Minnesota. This one is pretty close. I added chopped walnuts and dried cranberries! Great cookie to have handy in the freezer. Just slice and bake a dozen at a time! Baked them on parchment paper at 350 for 9-10 minutes",
            "datePublished": "2017-08-01T18:16:54.560Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
